The ten signs are synthetic, and are not a sign language
--------------------------------------------------------

The ten "reference signs" in this app are SYNTHETIC 21-point handshapes generated from a finger-extension
pattern and a wrist angle. They are not a recording of a real signer, they are not taken from any sign
language, and they are not a claim about how any Deaf community signs anything.

There is no trained sign-language recognition model in this app, and no camera. What ships is the mechanism:
ten references, a scale-normalised distance, a threshold, and an avatar drawn from a stored handshape.

Why "not recognised" matters
----------------------------

A hand further than the threshold from every reference returns "not recognised" and offers NO word. A small
vocabulary that guesses is worse than a small vocabulary that admits its limits: a wrong caption on a hand is
a wrong sentence about a person.
